03:20.770 --> 03:22.530
Enough. Next!

03:21.430 --> 03:23.010
<b>Not Evaluated</b>

03:23.520 --> 03:25.520
I will prepare a Grasshopper.

03:26.750 --> 03:30.150
In that case, I'll take it 
in pousse-café style.

03:30.410 --> 03:31.340
Huh?

03:31.340 --> 03:33.130
Surely you know what that is.

03:33.500 --> 03:35.010
Well, yes.

03:35.010 --> 03:38.940
It's a method for layering ingredients 
of different densities so they don't mix.

03:42.070 --> 03:44.880
A pro would have no trouble at all,

03:44.040 --> 03:45.290
<b></b>Stopwatch

03:44.040 --> 03:45.290
<b></b>Reset

03:44.040 --> 03:45.290
<b></b>Start

03:45.280 --> 03:47.520
but they got mixed up.

03:47.520 --> 03:49.710
And you took too long.

03:49.710 --> 03:52.260
I-I wasn't expecting an order like that.

03:52.260 --> 03:54.940
You must expect the customers to test you.

03:54.940 --> 03:55.790
Next!

03:58.870 --> 04:00.050
'Sup.

04:01.010 --> 04:02.530
Kurushima-kun...

04:03.080 --> 04:05.230
Was this one your idea?

04:05.230 --> 04:06.950
No, it was Higuchi-san's.

04:06.950 --> 04:09.700
He's all the buzz right now!

04:09.180 --> 04:10.030
So...

04:10.610 --> 04:13.590
That isn't what we're looking for.

04:10.800 --> 04:12.410
He's so cool!

04:15.150 --> 04:19.680
Why is Chief Kamishima 
always so prickly, anyway?

04:20.110 --> 04:23.210
No wonder the bartenders were upset.

04:24.050 --> 04:26.940
The hotel is already operating for business,

04:27.650 --> 04:31.660
but the bar still hasn't opened yet.

04:32.310 --> 04:35.000
At this rate, that door 
will never be unsealed.

04:35.890 --> 04:39.450
I never thought it would be 
this hard to find a bartender.

04:39.890 --> 04:43.970
It's making me as prickly as the chief. 
Giving me stomachaches, too.

04:44.560 --> 04:46.470
I'm jealous of you, Yukari-chan.

04:47.570 --> 04:51.210
You almost make it sound 
like I'm not working at all.

04:51.460 --> 04:54.080
I'm under pressure too, you know.

04:54.830 --> 04:57.070
I guess we start again from scratch.

04:57.070 --> 04:59.720
The search criteria are just too vague!

05:00.000 --> 05:02.670
And then he gets so picky 
over the littlest things.

05:02.670 --> 05:04.720
I mean, take a look at this!

05:04.740 --> 05:07.740
<b>Cocktail presentation</b>

05:04.740 --> 05:07.740
<b>Cocktail taste</b>

05:04.740 --> 05:07.740
<b>We need a bartender who can make the "Glass of God."</b>

05:04.980 --> 05:07.730
What even is a Glass of God?

05:07.730 --> 05:09.710
The chairman insists on it.

05:09.710 --> 05:13.250
Yeah, I know. But what 
is it supposed to mean?

05:13.250 --> 05:17.240
If we can't figure that out, that door 
really is going to stay sealed forever.

05:17.770 --> 05:19.460
You're probably right.

05:22.800 --> 05:25.530
The Glass of God, huh?

05:39.010 --> 05:41.270
Yes, yes? I'm coming!

05:42.020 --> 05:45.380
Um... Let's see...

05:48.010 --> 05:49.790
How does this thing work?

05:51.950 --> 05:54.580
Um, excuse me.

05:56.240 --> 05:59.010
Do you mind if I ask you something?

05:59.010 --> 06:00.280
Me?

06:00.280 --> 06:02.110
You have to swipe right here.

06:02.110 --> 06:03.010
Sue-wipe?

06:03.010 --> 06:03.690
Touch it.

06:03.690 --> 06:04.080
Okay.

06:04.080 --> 06:04.700
Then slide.

06:04.700 --> 06:05.320
Okay.

06:05.320 --> 06:07.870
Oh, yeah! You saved my neck! Thanks!

06:07.870 --> 06:09.490
<i>Hello? Hello?</i>

06:09.490 --> 06:10.860
Oh, hello? It's me.

06:10.860 --> 06:13.040
Oh, Maki-san? All right.

06:13.430 --> 06:14.880
What was up with him?

06:14.880 --> 06:17.260
What a disaster, Miwa-senpai.

06:18.570 --> 06:21.320
<b>Return By</b>

06:18.570 --> 06:21.320
<b></b>Bar Mania Press

06:18.910 --> 06:20.600
Did that guy leave this?

06:20.980 --> 06:23.400
Oh. Excuse me! Hey!

06:25.640 --> 06:26.690
He's gone.

06:27.780 --> 06:29.560
<i>Tokyo Bar Book</i>?

06:29.580 --> 06:30.620
<b></b>Bar Mania Press

06:29.920 --> 06:32.440
I wonder if this is...

06:32.450 --> 06:34.830
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

06:32.450 --> 06:34.830
<b>Return By\h\h\h\h\h\h

April 7 

1. TOKYO BAR BOOK
Bar Mania Press 
Item ID: 013648713012 




Minato-ku Library</b>

06:33.290 --> 06:34.830
<b>Azabu Area</b>

06:33.610 --> 06:34.810
It is.

06:35.280 --> 06:37.580
This is a library book.

06:37.580 --> 06:39.820
Huh? Oh, come on.

06:40.230 --> 06:42.820
Why is this happening?

06:44.150 --> 06:45.580
Please accept my apologies.

06:45.940 --> 06:48.350
Did they all fail again?

06:48.770 --> 06:51.830
Yes. That brings us to thirty people.

06:51.850 --> 06:56.100
<b>A Cat's</b>

06:52.100 --> 06:56.090
If he was easy to find, 
I would have done so long ago.

06:56.360 --> 07:01.110
Can you please at least provide me 
with more concrete criteria?

07:01.590 --> 07:05.510
What exactly is a Glass of God?

07:05.510 --> 07:07.840
Well, about that...

07:08.480 --> 07:09.990
"You'll know it when you drink it"?

07:08.490 --> 07:09.990
<b></b>Business Planning Division

07:10.860 --> 07:13.730
Are you sure that's what the chairman said?

07:13.730 --> 07:16.230
Why would I lie to you?

07:16.230 --> 07:19.030
But how can we search for that?

07:19.030 --> 07:21.200
Take your complaints to the chairman.

07:23.640 --> 07:27.250
We're the only ones stuck with this.

07:27.490 --> 07:28.260
Huh?

07:29.510 --> 07:32.730
Thanks to your coverage, our number 
of reservations has greatly increased.

07:32.730 --> 07:33.560
You're right.

07:33.560 --> 07:36.510
Regarding the event, correct? 
Yes, we would love to!

07:34.440 --> 07:36.510
Everyone's getting work done.

07:37.340 --> 07:40.070
At this rate, we'll be left behind.

07:40.400 --> 07:43.550
Anyway, we can't leave things like this.

07:43.550 --> 07:45.630
Find someone as soon as you can.

07:45.630 --> 07:46.490
Yes, sir!

07:50.530 --> 07:51.870
<b>Bar Hopper (bar_ztta)
1 hour ago
First drink of the day</b>

07:50.530 --> 07:52.530
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

07:51.870 --> 07:52.530
<b>Maru Maru @ Bartender (maru_BAR)
2 hours ago
Original cocktail ordered
by a regular customer


Watari Niwatori (toritarii)</b>

08:07.300 --> 08:09.550
<b></b>Trending

08:07.300 --> 08:09.550
<b>Calories!</b>

08:11.030 --> 08:12.470
Look this way!

08:12.470 --> 08:13.490
'Sup.

08:14.050 --> 08:15.720
'Sup!

08:18.060 --> 08:20.560
<b></b>Sumida River

08:20.560 --> 08:22.560
<b>Ogura</b>

08:21.520 --> 08:22.920
What?!

08:22.920 --> 08:25.920
What do you mean, expenses aren't covered?

08:25.920 --> 08:28.840
Accounting said they won't pay any more.

08:28.840 --> 08:33.800
You mean we have to pay for all of it? 
There goes my salary!

08:33.800 --> 08:35.560
You still haven't found someone

08:35.890 --> 08:37.880
to be the bartender behind that sealed door?

08:37.880 --> 08:39.720
That's right.

08:39.720 --> 08:42.190
We may never find one.

08:42.190 --> 08:44.560
Do you know anyone?

08:44.560 --> 08:47.820
Any bartenders who can 
make the "Glass of God"?

08:49.520 --> 08:50.570
Sure I do.

08:50.570 --> 08:51.370
Huh?

08:51.370 --> 08:53.470
Where? Where is he?

08:54.360 --> 08:55.850
He's right here.

08:57.320 --> 09:02.050
I keep this place open so late, 
it basically makes me a god.

09:02.050 --> 09:04.840
Would you please refrain 
from the unfunny jokes?

09:04.840 --> 09:07.110
Is that how you talk to a god?

09:07.110 --> 09:08.850
In that case,

09:08.850 --> 09:11.890
if you're a god, get our expenses paid!

09:11.890 --> 09:13.440
Hey. Welcome.

09:13.440 --> 09:15.480
Hello. Highball, please.

09:16.950 --> 09:18.070
Are you...?

09:19.070 --> 09:19.860
Oh?

09:19.860 --> 09:21.970
It <i>is</i> you! From before!

09:21.970 --> 09:23.610
The guy who can't use a smartphone!

09:23.930 --> 09:26.810
Yeah, I'm no good with those.

09:26.810 --> 09:31.310
Oh, right. Did you happen to see a book? 
I might have forgotten it there.

09:31.310 --> 09:33.050
Yes, I have it.

09:33.050 --> 09:34.120
Really?

09:34.120 --> 09:37.860
I don't have it on me right now, 
but I'll return it for you.

09:37.860 --> 09:39.870
The library is near my office.

09:40.180 --> 09:42.890
Will you? Thank you so much!

09:43.280 --> 09:46.360
I guess I shouldn't give up on Japan just yet.

09:47.020 --> 09:48.470
Here, your highball.

09:48.470 --> 09:50.820
Ah, great. Thank you.

09:51.410 --> 09:54.580
This is so weak! You call this a highball?

09:54.580 --> 09:56.840
Did you skimp on the whisky?

09:56.840 --> 09:59.410
The ice melted because 
you weren't drinking it.

09:59.710 --> 10:03.910
Oh, right. Speaking of bartenders, 
this guy is a bartender too.

10:03.910 --> 10:05.160
Huh?

10:05.160 --> 10:07.990
I wanted to thank you for before.

10:07.990 --> 10:08.610
Oh.

10:08.610 --> 10:14.450
Senpai, this must be fate. 
Let's get him to take the bartender test.

10:15.670 --> 10:18.870
Kinda silly to have forgotten your wallet.

10:18.870 --> 10:22.310
I'm so sorry. But I remembered it today.

10:22.660 --> 10:24.640
Oh. I forgot to go to the bank.

10:24.640 --> 10:26.180
Or maybe not.

10:26.180 --> 10:27.140
Definitely.

10:28.900 --> 10:31.050
But where are we going to find him?

10:31.840 --> 10:34.370
Our bartender...

10:44.830 --> 10:46.830
<b></b>Ginza Shopping Center

10:44.830 --> 10:46.830
<b></b>Ginza M's Building

11:02.280 --> 11:05.090
Edenhall in Ginza?

11:05.090 --> 11:11.610
Yes. It says the bartender there once 
won a cocktail competition in Europe.

11:07.350 --> 11:11.610
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

11:07.350 --> 11:11.610
<b>Bar Hopper
Local Guide - 1024 Reviews

A great place to enjoy drinks.
He'll pinpoint your tastes and thrill you.
The service is excellent.
You'll want to keep going back
knowing that each time you do,
he'll thrill you with new pleasures.
The bartender is named Sasakura.
He won a cocktail competition
in Europe and has top-notch skills.

taka yamano

...but at some point they reopened.</b>

11:11.590 --> 11:15.280
Wasn't Edenhall supposed to have closed down?

11:11.610 --> 11:13.610
<b>Ginza</b>

11:15.280 --> 11:20.870
It says, "The private bar with the 
irregular schedule finally reopened."

11:20.870 --> 11:25.620
It's a private bar? If he's so amazing, 
then why's it private?

11:25.860 --> 11:30.510
It does sound a little strange, 
but it might be worth a visit.

11:30.510 --> 11:32.120
If our expenses are covered.

11:32.350 --> 11:33.620
You're right.

11:33.930 --> 11:35.850
If our expenses are covered.

11:40.000 --> 11:41.510
Fine. Here's a donation.

11:42.200 --> 11:44.640
Thank you very much!

11:42.550 --> 11:44.630
Yes! You're a saint, Chief Kamishima!

11:46.560 --> 11:50.680
Well, it should be around here.

11:52.130 --> 11:54.260
Oh, is that it over there?

11:52.150 --> 11:55.150
<b></b>Ginza Shopping Center

11:52.150 --> 11:55.150
<b></b>Ginza M's Building

11:55.260 --> 11:56.540
See?

11:56.240 --> 11:58.160
<b></b>French

11:56.240 --> 11:58.160
<b></b>Ginza Shopping Center

11:56.540 --> 12:00.290
I've been down this street 
more times than I remember,

12:00.290 --> 12:02.150
but I never even noticed this place.

12:30.200 --> 12:32.650
It sure seems like a nice place.

12:33.310 --> 12:34.710
Yeah, maybe.

12:35.910 --> 12:38.720
Sasakura-kun, you have customers.

12:39.070 --> 12:40.680
Certainly. On my way.

12:44.880 --> 12:45.740
Oh!

12:48.100 --> 12:49.250
Welcome.

12:49.250 --> 12:51.260
It's you... again?

12:51.260 --> 12:53.730
Oh. We keep running into each other.

12:54.090 --> 12:56.080
Thank you for your help the other day.

12:56.440 --> 12:57.980
Please, take a seat.

12:57.980 --> 12:59.360
O-Okay.

13:00.880 --> 13:02.560
Acquaintances of yours?

13:02.560 --> 13:04.730
Yes, well, sort of.

13:04.730 --> 13:08.180
He seems kind of different from before.

13:16.910 --> 13:19.100
Senpai, what do you think?

13:19.800 --> 13:23.120
It is an impressive selection.

13:23.510 --> 13:24.400
Here you are.

13:26.040 --> 13:27.430
Thanks.

13:27.780 --> 13:30.160
I'm surprised you found this place.

13:30.160 --> 13:32.430
Did you ask the owner of Ogura?

13:32.430 --> 13:34.670
I found reviews online

13:34.950 --> 13:37.920
talking about an incredibly skilled bartender.

13:38.140 --> 13:41.360
Oh? Have people been saying that?

13:43.420 --> 13:45.850
Well, what would you like?

13:44.490 --> 13:48.200
<i>So he really was a bartender.</i>

13:45.850 --> 13:48.200
Hmm. Let me think a minute.

13:48.970 --> 13:51.880
<i>I wonder if the reviews are accurate.</i>

13:52.780 --> 13:55.920
Sasakura-kun, I'll take a Grasshopper.

13:56.270 --> 13:59.940
Certainly. Shall I prepare it 
pousse-café style?

14:00.360 --> 14:02.140
That is nice once in a while.

14:02.140 --> 14:04.540
Pousse-café? Like the one from the test?

14:14.820 --> 14:17.700
Here you are. Your Grasshopper.

14:17.710 --> 14:19.460
<b></b>Stopwatch

14:17.710 --> 14:19.460
<b></b>Reset

14:17.710 --> 14:19.460
<b></b>Start

14:17.710 --> 14:19.460
<b></b>Lap 1

14:17.950 --> 14:19.450
Thirty seconds?!

14:19.450 --> 14:23.090
That's pretty amazing, right? 
And it isn't mixed at all.

14:23.090 --> 14:24.240
You're right.

14:25.570 --> 14:26.550
Your chaser.

14:26.550 --> 14:27.150
Thanks.

14:27.150 --> 14:28.410
<i>In that case...</i>

14:28.410 --> 14:29.770
Um...

14:29.770 --> 14:31.710
Yes? Have you decided?

14:31.710 --> 14:34.460
I'd like a martini, please.

14:34.790 --> 14:36.300
A martini?

14:39.250 --> 14:41.220
It appears you haven't dined yet.

14:41.710 --> 14:46.730
Perhaps you would prefer a lighter beverage 
with a lower percentage of alcohol?

14:47.100 --> 14:49.530
I guess that would be the correct move.

14:50.450 --> 14:56.240
Then please make me something lighter 
than a martini. Something shaken, please.

14:56.240 --> 14:58.150
Oh, and colored pink.

14:58.770 --> 15:00.360
As you wish.

15:20.980 --> 15:25.650
I don't know why, but when I see a 
hard-working man use his fingers like that,

15:27.930 --> 15:29.880
it's super sexy!

15:29.880 --> 15:31.640
Uh, sexy?

15:36.330 --> 15:39.170
Here you are. A Cosmopolitan.

15:44.150 --> 15:47.410
Wow! This is really delicious!

15:47.710 --> 15:49.020
It's that good?

15:49.020 --> 15:50.410
It really is!

15:52.240 --> 15:54.160
And what would you like?

15:53.390 --> 15:55.120
This is so good!

15:58.170 --> 15:59.200
<i>If...</i>

15:59.680 --> 16:03.050
<i>If this person truly is 
an amazing bartender...</i>

16:04.660 --> 16:06.110
Whatever you recommend.

16:07.140 --> 16:11.900
Senpai, you shouldn't do that. 
It really puts bartenders on the spot.

16:12.340 --> 16:13.680
<i>That's right.</i>

16:13.680 --> 16:19.190
<i>He doesn't know if I prefer strong drinks, 
or what kinds of liquor I don't like.</i>

16:19.760 --> 16:23.550
<i>He doesn't know enough about me 
to know what to make.</i>

16:24.270 --> 16:27.210
<i>And that's exactly why 
it will test his skills.</i>

16:27.600 --> 16:28.990
Whatever you recommend.

16:28.990 --> 16:31.910
Please make a cocktail that you 
think would be perfect for me.

16:33.420 --> 16:34.770
Very well.

17:00.480 --> 17:02.360
<i>A whisky base.</i>

17:02.880 --> 17:07.910
<i>With a whisky base, the obvious choices 
would be a Manhattan or a Godfather.</i>

17:08.380 --> 17:11.660
<i>Or in that glass, a Whisky Buck.</i>

17:12.170 --> 17:15.240
<i>Since he's using scotch, 
maybe a Highland Cooler.</i>

17:20.010 --> 17:21.170
<i>Soda?</i>

17:22.490 --> 17:24.720
<i>Whisky and soda?</i>

17:29.010 --> 17:30.260
Isn't that just...

17:31.800 --> 17:33.280
A highball.

17:33.970 --> 17:38.100
<i>A highball? That's the perfect drink for me?</i>

17:39.120 --> 17:42.620
<i>It's just whisky diluted in soda.</i>

17:43.560 --> 17:47.550
<i>Anyone could make something like that.</i>

17:50.560 --> 17:52.430
Let's drink these and leave.

17:53.170 --> 17:54.300
Senpai?

17:54.900 --> 17:56.020
<i>It turns out</i>

17:56.540 --> 17:58.640
<i>I was let down after all.</i>

17:59.560 --> 18:01.900
<i>We'll have to start the 
search all over again.</i>

18:15.860 --> 18:18.960
It has such a smooth, gentle flavor.

18:19.790 --> 18:21.910
Is this really just a highball?

18:23.050 --> 18:23.850
Yes.

18:24.550 --> 18:27.960
And yet, it is a delicious highball.

18:32.670 --> 18:34.950
Why is it so good?

18:35.600 --> 18:37.300
In this world,

18:37.300 --> 18:42.080
there are two types of professions that 
absolutely must not deceive the customer.

18:42.690 --> 18:45.370
One is the physician or pharmacist.

18:45.920 --> 18:47.460
And the other is...

18:48.130 --> 18:49.720
The other is...?

18:50.820 --> 18:52.060
The bartender.

18:52.590 --> 18:54.620
In either job, one small 
change to the formula

18:54.620 --> 18:57.930
is the difference between 
serving poison or medicine.

18:57.930 --> 18:59.260
Medicine?

19:01.450 --> 19:03.450
I have an exhausted customer.

19:04.260 --> 19:07.640
She has been so busy with work, 
she can't pay attention to anything else.

19:08.220 --> 19:10.690
Such as a loose sleeve button.

19:11.600 --> 19:13.290
It appears it finally came off.

19:16.720 --> 19:19.270
You're also wearing your watch differently.

19:19.270 --> 19:22.250
Huh? How did you...?

19:23.090 --> 19:23.890
Was it...

19:25.120 --> 19:26.720
that one time before?

19:28.060 --> 19:32.150
You paid attention to such tiny details
and remembered them?

19:33.860 --> 19:36.800
For a body under so much stress,

19:36.800 --> 19:40.730
I felt a normal highball 
recipe would be too strong.

19:41.070 --> 19:43.910
So I reduced the amount of alcohol.

19:44.270 --> 19:48.430
No way. Then why isn't the flavor any weaker?

19:48.430 --> 19:49.410
It's the ice.

19:49.920 --> 19:52.870
Although I reduced the 
alcohol as much as I could,

19:52.870 --> 19:55.650
I used hard ice to maintain 
the flavor balance.

19:56.480 --> 20:00.500
If you freeze ice over a long period, 
it becomes even harder.

20:00.960 --> 20:05.670
Then, if you cut out the core parts and 
rest them in a freezer for a few days,

20:07.690 --> 20:10.420
the ice becomes denser and harder to melt.

20:11.790 --> 20:16.380
You put this much thought 
into just one drink?

20:17.690 --> 20:21.680
Do you know the meaning 
of the word "bartender"?

20:23.400 --> 20:27.060
A "bar" is a perch upon which to rest. 
"Tender" means gentle or kind.

20:27.060 --> 20:29.790
So bartender means a "gentle perch."

20:30.860 --> 20:34.070
This is merely a piece of wood 
to place liquor on. A bar.

20:34.910 --> 20:37.490
But there is also a bartender here.

20:38.310 --> 20:41.890
Bar and tender. A place 
where tenderness grows.

20:43.520 --> 20:45.700
So that explains this highball.

20:46.630 --> 20:50.960
And here I was trying to test you.

20:51.770 --> 20:57.540
I want the customer on the other side of the
counter to enjoy the perfect drink for them.

20:57.980 --> 21:00.580
Really, that's all there is to it.

21:05.400 --> 21:07.240
We've finally found him!

21:07.240 --> 21:11.740
Sasakura Ryu. I'm sure the 
chairman will like him, too!

21:07.250 --> 21:11.750
<b>Ginza</b>

21:11.740 --> 21:15.250
Chief bartender at the Ratz Hotel in Paris.

21:11.750 --> 21:15.260
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

21:11.750 --> 21:15.260
<b><u>Sasakura Ryu (29 Years Old)

</u>Served as chief bartender at Sky Bar,
a bar on the top floor of the five-star
Ratz Hotel in the outskirts of Paris.
Took top prize at the International
Cocktail Competition in Europe.
After returning to Japan, went back
to work as a bartender at Edenhall
in Ginza.

Points of Investigation
* Assessment in Paris in addition
to experiences after returning
* Accomplishments in Japan
before going overseas
* Assessment at Edenhall</b>

21:15.710 --> 21:17.470
So he lived abroad?

21:17.950 --> 21:20.490
No wonder he wasn't picked up as a candidate.

21:20.490 --> 21:23.990
I know he's the one who 
can make the Glass of God!

21:23.990 --> 21:26.000
You'll know it when you drink it, too, Chief!

21:26.000 --> 21:27.240
Are you sure?

21:27.810 --> 21:31.270
But why did he come back to Japan?

21:31.270 --> 21:34.110
I was wondering about that myself.

21:34.110 --> 21:38.010
That's beside the point. The problem is 
whether or not he'll come work for us.

21:38.290 --> 21:41.190
And whether or not he measures up 
to the chairman's expectations.

21:41.190 --> 21:42.850
Hurry up and put a proposal together.

21:42.850 --> 21:43.520
Yes, sir!

21:44.870 --> 21:46.130
Okay.

21:49.420 --> 21:50.780
What's this?

21:51.950 --> 21:54.780
Huh? Weren't you going to return it?

21:54.780 --> 21:57.720
I totally forgot!

23:45.110 --> 23:50.070
<b>Episode 2</b>

23:45.110 --> 23:50.070
<b>Old Pal</b>
